==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːvəl}}

===Etymology===
From Middle English {{term|wevel|lang=enm}}, from Old English {{term|wifel|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|wibilaz}} (cf. Dutch tort{{term|tortwevel|wevel|lang=nl}} ‘dung beetle’, Low German Scharn''wevel'' ‘id.’, German {{term|Wiebel|lang=de}} ‘beetle, chafer’), from {{proto|Indo-European|webʰel}} (cf. Lithuanian {{term|vãbalas|lang=lt}} ‘beetle, weevil’, Russian dialect {{term|веблица|tr=veblica||intestinal worm|lang=ru}}), from {{proto|Indo-European|webʰ-||h₁webʰ-|to weave, wave|lang=en}}. More at {{l|en|weave}} and {{l|en|wave}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several small [[herbivorous]] [[beetle|beetles]] in the superfamily [[Curculionoidea]]. Many of them have a distinctive snout.
# Any of several small herbivorous beetles in the family [[Curculionidae]] belonging to the superfamily ''Curculionoidea''.
# Any of several similar but more distantly related beetles such as the [[biscuit weevil]].

